power: supply: qcom_pm8150b: bring the charger up on the OnePlus 8 Pro

The ROCKNIX 0011 driver (with its safe float-voltage formula) stays as
the base; this patch rewrites it to the state Nura (formerly
postmarketOS) runs on this very device, i.e. the pmOS soc tree base
(sm8250-7.2.0_git20261010) plus Nura's fix chain:

  0068 float voltage encoding (already present in ROCKNIX's copy,
      re-applied harmlessly by the rewrite)
  0073 read USB telemetry while charging is paused
  0082 release the wake IRQ on detach
  0083 scale the USB input current
  0084 report battery overvoltage
  0085 follow TCPM limits and refresh on source change
  0165 keep at least 500 mA of USB input while VBUS is present
  0166 charge by the external fuel gauge like the stock firmware
      (temperature zones, early-cycle restart; fixes the ~88 % stall;
      keyed off the "qcom,fuel-gauge" phandle, our DTS points it at
      the bq27541)

Source: darknagel/oneplus-instantnoodlep-nura-unofficial
kernel-patches 0068/0073/0082/0083/0084/0085/0165/0166, applied onto
the pmOS base file, then diffed against ROCKNIX 0011's copy.
